  "title": "Ex 7.10 · a³ ≡ a (mod 3)",
  "prompt": "Let $a$ be an integer. Prove that $a^3 \\equiv a \\pmod 3$, that is, $3 \\mid (a^3 - a)$. Split into cases by the remainder of $a$ when divided by 3.",
  "answer_format": "A structured proof: let, case, expr and witness steps (notes optional). No final answer box. Use case steps to split into possibilities.",
